{"metadata":{"title":"GameText.Holding","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Holding","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV7HoldingV","roleHeading":"Structure","extendedModule":"Gnusto","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Holding","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A thing and what holds it: what the player put down, and the box, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"table or the hamper it went into."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/holding"]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Holding\/holder","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Holding\/item"]},{"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Holding\/samples"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DroppableSubject","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/LineSubject","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/NamedSubject","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Holding"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextAndRandomness"]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line"},{"type":"text","text":" is about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"one","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" object, and a sentence about two needs some way"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to say which is which. The roles are a type rather than a pair, because"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the pair spelling — a tuple, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$0"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$1"},{"type":"text","text":" — leaves the API unable to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answer the only question an author actually asks at the call site: which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one is the container? "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\($0.holder)"},{"type":"text","text":" answers it; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\($1)"},{"type":"text","text":" does not."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One struct serves every line whose two things stand in this relation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than one apiece — which is also what lets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RoomDescriber"},{"type":"text","text":" keep"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handing "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/itemOnSurface"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/itemInContainer"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one helper as a value. Another such line should cost no edit here."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Line"},{"type":"text","text":" over one of these is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ExpressibleByStringLiteral"},{"type":"text","text":", so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two-object line will take a fixed sentence — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text.putItemIn = \"Done.\""},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"— and print it without either name. For these that is a legitimate thing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a game to want, and the sentence it prints is still true. It is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"legitimate for a line whose whole content is the thing it was handed,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is why these are "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DroppableSubject"},{"type":"text","text":"s and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Word"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its neighbours are not."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["text.putItemIn = .naming { \"You tuck \\($0.item) into \\($0.holder).\" }"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both arrive as "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Noun"},{"type":"text","text":" for the reason one does — and for a second reason"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a one-object line never has. A sentence about two things has two things"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its verb might agree with, and it is rarely the one the sentence names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/itemOnSurface"},{"type":"text","text":" reads “On the table are the rails”,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where the verb agrees with the rails and the template names the table."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"While these were a pair of strings there was no way to write that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sentence at all."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Holding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText"]]},"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameText"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText","title":"GameText","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GameText"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every stock player-facing line the engine can say, as one overridable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value — so a game can speak in its own voice without touching behavior."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s16SendableMetatypeP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/Word":{"abstract":[{"text":"A fragment of what the player typed, quoted back at them.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/word","title":"GameText.Word","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Word"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Word"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Word","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/Noun":{"title":"GameText.Noun","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/noun","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rendered noun phrase that also knows its own number, for the lines"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose verb has to agree with it."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","t